{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>To the south.</b> This is the banner-camp of Reuven. One might think: just as he blows for the east and for the south, so he blows for the north and for the west — Scripture says, ״תרועה יתקעו למסעיהן״ — they blow for the journey of those two camps specifically, and in honor of the Mishkan, which travels after these two banners. Another interpretation: he blows for all four camps." "<b>And you shall blow a teru'ah a second time.</b> From here you learn that they would blow קר״ק (teqi'ah–teru'ah–teqi'ah)." "<b>And you shall blow a teru'ah a second time.</b> Rashi explained: a sign for the journey of the camps — teqi'ah, teru'ah, and teqi'ah — so it is expounded in the Sifrei from the superfluous verses. And this is what it says: it says regarding the east wind ״תרועה״ and it says regarding the south wind ״תרועה״ — just as ״תרועה״ there means ״they shall blow,״ so too the ״תרועה״ stated regarding the east means a teqi'ah after the teru'ah. And just as for the east wind there is a teqi'ah before the teru'ah, as it is written ״ותקעתם תרועה,״ so too that stated for the south is a teqi'ah before the teru'ah. And if you ask: why is the verse needed? For regarding the east, we learn from it that there is a teqi'ah before the teru'ah for the south — but for the south itself, a teqi'ah before the teru'ah is written, as it is written <b>ותקעתם תרועה שנית</b> — one may answer: if the verse regarding the east, ״ותקעתם תרועה,״ had not been written, I would have said that for the south they would blow teqi'ah and two teru'ot and teqi'ah, since regarding the south it is written ״ותקעתם תרועה שנית תרועה יתקעו״; therefore the verse regarding the east is needed to learn from it that for the south there is a teqi'ah before the teru'ah. There you have it: קר״ק."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {2 "The second comment explicitly cites Rashi; the first comment's closing וי״א (ואיכא דאמרי / 'and some say') introduces an unnamed alternative view, here rendered 'another interpretation' per the compiler's idiom."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:18.324807204Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}